| *************** Squashing a Commit *************** |
---

---

Git has the ability squashing commits on a branch that HAS NOT BEEN PULLED YET and combine commits into 1 commit.
This is typically when a developer has created a load a commits whist developing a feature and wants to group the commits into one sensibel commit.

## Syntax

    $ git reset --soft HEAD~<Number of commits to sqaush>
    $ git commit -m "<New commit message>"
    $ git push --force origin <branch name>

## Example: A feature branch (feature/implementHelloWorld) has 10 commits that need sqashing into 1

    $ git reset --soft HEAD~10
    $ git commit -m "Hello World Code"
    $ git push --force	feature/implementHelloWorld
